  "result": "Perfect! All 143 tests pass (119 original + 24 new dates tests). Here's what I implemented:\n\n\u2705 **Created `src/dates.js`** with three UTC-based date functions:\n\n1. **`isValidDate(text)`**\n   - Validates that a string is in 'YYYY-MM-DD' format\n   - Checks that the date actually exists (rejects Feb 30, etc.)\n   - Uses UTC (T00:00:00Z) for all date operations\n   - Handles leap years correctly\n\n2. **`addDays(date, n)`**\n   - Adds n days to a date string (n can be negative)\n   - Returns result as 'YYYY-MM-DD' string with zero-padding\n   - Works across month and year boundaries\n   - Uses UTC for calculations\n\n3. **`daysBetween(a, b)`**\n   - Calculates whole days between two dates (b minus a)\n   - Returns positive for b > a, negative for b < a, zero for same date\n   - Uses UTC-based calculation\n   - Throws on invalid date formats\n\n\u2705 **Updated `createInvoice`** to use `isValidDate` from dates.js\n\n\u2705 **Comprehensive tests** (24 new) covering:\n- Valid and invalid date formats\n- Leap year handling (Feb 29 in 2024, not 2025)\n- Day addition across boundaries (month/year)\n- Negative day subtraction\n- `daysBetween` calculations\n- Error handling for invalid formats\n- Inverse operations (`addDays` + `daysBetween` consistency)\n- Large positive/negative offsets\n\n\u2705 **Decision implemented:** All dates are 'YYYY-MM-DD' strings everywhere, and all date arithmetic uses UTC, never the machine's local timezone.",
